Hi Mihoko,

Please find attached proposal MLP-202504-PRO-001 with the two options and the=
ir fee breakdowns.

The company-wide option is 20 taught hours per person for 178 employees in te=
n classes of up to 18, at =C2=A54,400,000. Participants would review session =
material outside class; that time is additional to the taught hours.

The shorter option is priced for your 18 customer enquiry staff as one class.=
 It includes four two-hour sessions per person, at =C2=A5320,000, and does no=
t assume individual homework or preparation outside class. The pair practice =
takes the enquiry through to a handover to Sales.

Both fees are in yen excluding tax. For either option, Mirai would provide th=
e venue and arrange work schedules and coverage. We can agree dates and the d=
etailed timetable before delivery.

Best wishes,
Diane Mitchell
Milton Learning Partners

On 7 April 2025 at 16:12, Mihoko Sato wrote:
> Hi Diane,
>
> Could you put together two options that we can compare by 10 April? One wou=
ld be the longer programme for all employees. The other would be a shorter co=
urse for the 18 people at our customer enquiry desk, focusing on the first re=
sponse only: asking about the enquiry, preferred date and number of participa=
nts, giving a time for our reply, and passing the details to Sales.
>
> For each option, could you separate the training hours per person, the maxi=
mum number who can be taught together, the fee in yen before tax, and whether=
 any preparation outside class is required? That will help us compare both th=
e cost and the time away from work.
>
> Thank you,
> Mihoko Sato

